From 068df64beaf19f3b7f0cd54e1834230c34077539 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:48:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] v4l2object: Don't probe colorimetry for compressed
 formats on OUTPUT

A UVC camera's MJPEG stream can't be decoded with v4l2jpegdec:

  v4l2src ! image/jpeg,width=3840,height=2160 ! jpegparse ! v4l2jpegdec ! ...
  WARN GST_CAPS pre_eventfunc_check:<v4l2jpegdec0:sink> caps image/jpeg, ...
       colorimetry=(string)2:4:5:1, ... not accepted
  streaming stopped, reason not-negotiated (-4)

The camera (uvcvideo) reports sRGB, a BT.709 transfer function, the
BT.601 matrix and the default quantization. GStreamer turns that into
2:4:5:1. The decoder's sink caps carry a colorimetry list that
gst_v4l2_object_add_colorspace() probed with TRY_FMT. To avoid flooding
slow devices with ioctls, it tries only the standard colorspaces and a
few variants of them, so the list contains combinations such as
1:4:7:1, but not this valid one. The caps intersection then fails,
although rkjpegd accepts the format, with its quantization, in TRY_FMT.

For a compressed format on an OUTPUT queue, i.e. the bitstream fed to a
decoder, the colorimetry describes the stream. The driver carries it over
to the CAPTURE side and doesn't choose it. A probed closed list adds
nothing there, and it rejects valid streams. Skip the probe in that case,
so the sink caps leave the colorimetry unconstrained. Capture
queues and raw formats are unchanged.

Reproducer (Aluratek UHD 4K camera, RK3588 rkjpegd):
  gst-launch-1.0 v4l2src device=/dev/video10 num-buffers=60 !
    image/jpeg,width=3840,height=2160,framerate=30/1 ! jpegparse !
    v4l2jpegdec ! fakevideosink
fails with not-negotiated before the change and decodes every frame
after it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c b/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c
index 53f4e08..8016171 100644
--- a/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c
@@ -2666,6 +2666,20 @@ gst_v4l2_object_add_colorspace (GstV4l2Object * v4l2object, GstStructure * s,
   GstVideoColorimetry cinfo;
   enum v4l2_colorspace req_cspace;
 
+  /* The colorimetry of a compressed bitstream fed to a decoder is a property
+   * of the stream: the driver only carries it over to the CAPTURE queue. A
+   * probed list is limited to the standard combinations tried below, so it
+   * would reject valid streams such as a UVC camera's MJPEG with 2:4:5:1
+   * (sRGB, BT.601 matrix, BT.709 transfer, default quantization). Leave the
+   * colorimetry unconstrained there. */
+  if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT (v4l2object->type)) {
+    struct v4l2_fmtdesc *desc =
+        gst_v4l2_object_get_format_from_fourcc (v4l2object, pixelformat);
+
+    if (desc && (desc->flags & V4L2_FMT_FLAG_COMPRESSED))
+      return;
+  }
+
   memset (&fmt, 0, sizeof (fmt));
   fmt.type = v4l2object->type;
   fmt.fmt.pix.width = width;
-- 
